Principles on Management and Utilization
The management and utilization of ERF shall adhere to the following principles:
1. Centralized and uniform in accordance to the Government Accounting system;
2. Ensure fund utilization is consistent with the objectives, economical, efficient and
sustainable;
3. [Ensure] agility, quickness, fairness, transparency, openness and auditability;
4. All revenues and expenditures shall operate through the accounting system, as
well as receive regular monitoring, inspection and audit in accordance with the laws.

Revenue Sources of Emergency Relief Fund
  The revenue sources of ERF come from:
1. Contribution from the Government;
2. Voluntary contribution from individuals, entities [and] organizations, both
domestic and foreign;
3. Technical operations and resource mobilization activities;
4. Interest gain from deposit [account] and revenue from the management of ERF;
5. Other legal revenues in accordance to the laws and regulations.

Objectives of the Utilization of Emergency Relief Fund
   ERF shall be utilized for the following objectives:
1. Emergency rescue;
2. Emergency relief;
3. Preparedness for emergency assistance;
4. Conduct emergency assistance fundraising activity;
5. Management and administration of ERF;
6. Other objectives related to emergency assistance work as agreed by the Board of
Directors of ERF.

Location of the Emergency Relief Fund
ERF at each level has the following location:
1. At the central level, it is located at the Lao Red Cross;
2. At the provincial level, it is located at the Provincial, Capital Red Cross Branch;
3. At the district level, it is located at the District, Municipality, City Red Cross
Branch.

Personnel structure of the Board of Directors of Emergency Relief Fund
 The Board of Directors of ERF at the central level has a personnel structure as
following:
1. President of Lao Red Cross








Chair;
2. Vice President of Lao Red Cross        Vice-Chair, as well as a Standing Member;
3. Director General of State Budget Department, Ministry of Finance  Vice-Chair;
4. Director of Cabinet Office of Lao Red Cross
    Member;
5. Representative of the Ministry of Labor and Social Welfare
    Member;
6. Representative of the Prime Minister Office



    Member;
7. Representative of the Lao Red Cross Honorary Members

    Member;
8. Director of Fundraising and Disaster Management Office

    Member,






as well as Head of the Secretariat.

As for the personnel structure of the Board of Directors of ERF at the provincial and
district level, it is established in a separate regulation.
Personnel of the Board of Directors of ERF at each level shall not receive salary or
wage from ERF for the performance of their duties, other than meeting allowances or other
benefits as established in the regulations of the Ministry of Finance.

Rights and Duties of the Board of Directors of Emergency Relief Fund
The Board of Directors of ERF at each level has the following rights and duties:
1.
Govern and manage ERF, including implement the mobilization of emergency
assistance within the scope of its responsibilities;
2.
Consider and endorse the internal rules, operation plans, reports [and] annual
budget plans of ERF;
3.
Consider and endorse the programs, projects and activities of ERF;
4. Lead [and] provide guidance on resource mobilization and fundraising from
individuals, entities [and] organizations, both domestic and foreign;
5. Appoint the Secretariat of ERF;
6. Consider [and] endorse regulations on the management and operation of ERF;
7. Examine, consider [and] approve the utilization of ERF;
8. Propose to the higher-level Board of Directors of ERF to consider the approval of
emergency assistance fund, in the case where funding of ERF at its level is
insufficient;
9. Monitor, inspect and evaluate the utilization of ERF according to [its] objectives,
plans and budget plans, in order to attain transparency, efficiency and
effectiveness;
10. Endorse the financial audit results of ER;
11. Conclude and report on the operation of ERF to its higher-level authorities at least
once per year;
12. Exercise other rights and perform other duties as stipulated in the laws and
regulations.

Rights and Duties of the Secretariat
The Secretariat of ERF at each level has the following rights and duties:
1. Support the Board of Directors of ERF in governing and managing the operation
and accounting-finance of ERF;
2. Examine [and] develop the internal rules, annual operation plans, reports and
annual budget plans to propose to the Board of Directors of ERF for consideration;
3. Examine [and] develop the programs, projects and activities to propose to the
Board of Directors of ERF for consideration;
4. Examine [and] develop regulations on the governance and management of ERF,
then propose to the Board of Directors for consideration;
5. Approve the utilization of ERF when emergency event takes place, as determined
by the Board of Directors of ERF;
6. Disseminate the regulations on ERF;
7. Govern and manage the operation of ERF to [ensure] alignment with the
objectives in a transparent and effective manner;
8. Study [and] examine the methodologies and forms of resource mobilization, from
both domestic and international [sources], including implement resource mobilization and
fundraising activities for ERF;
9. Record [and] document the revenue-expenditure of ERF, manage the assets [and]
funding received from contributions and various sources of revenue, as well as manage the
deposit account of ERF with transparency and auditability;
10. Disburse funding and materials to support the implementation of various
activities in accordance with the endorsed plans;
11. Monitor, inspect and evaluate the utilization of funding and materials by various
approved parties;
12. Collaborate with relevant parties on the implementation of emergency assistance
work;
13. Conclude and report on the operation of ERF to the Board of Directors of ERF
on a regular basis;
14. Exercise other rights and duties as stipulated in the laws and as assigned by the
Board of Directors of ERF;

